{"title":"Mr. Arkadin","original_title":"Mr. Arkadin","directors":["Orson Welles"],"cast_top":["Orson Welles","Akim Tamiroff","Grégoire Aslan","Patricia Medina","Jack Watling","Mischa Auer","Peter van Eyck","Michael Redgrave"],"genres":["mystery","thriller"],"keywords":["neo-noir"],"overview":"Claiming that he doesn't know his own past, a rich man enlists an ex-con with an odd bit of detective work. Gregory Arkadin says he can't remember anything before the late 1920s, and convict Guy Van Stratten is happy to take the job of exploring his new acquaintance's life story.","release_year":1955,"runtime_minutes":107,"original_language":"en","poster_path":"/hoBfh3jmA3XDDx9tGgMwdGd37GE.jpg","backdrop_path":"/dSBvYxsJnfIVqpkVu1xDSVSsMvv.jpg","tmdb_id":44026},
{"title":"The Children Are Watching Us","original_title":"I bambini ci guardano","directors":["Vittorio De Sica"],"cast_top":["Emilio Cigoli","Luciano De Ambrosis","Isa Pola","Adriano Rimoldi","Giovanna Cigoli","Jone Frigerio","Maria Gardena","Dina Perbellini"],"genres":["drama"],"keywords":["innocence"],"overview":"In his first collaboration with renowned screenwriter and longtime partner Cesare Zavattini, Vittorio De Sica examines the cataclysmic consequences of adult folly on an innocent child. Heralding the pair’s subsequent work on some of the masterpieces of Italian neorealism, The Children Are Watching Us is a vivid, deeply humane portrait of a family’s disintegration.","release_year":1943,"runtime_minutes":84,"original_language":"it","poster_path":"/vEkp2FoxUFpCGeioWdUS4wb7ezh.jpg","backdrop_path":"/jlUSRGkcPDNYAhxlezdohFHrDCa.jpg","tmdb_id":61461},
