{"title":"Lacombe, Lucien","original_title":"Lacombe Lucien","directors":["Louis Malle"],"cast_top":["Pierre Blaise","Aurore Clément","Holger Löwenadler","Therese Giehse","Stéphane Bouy","Loumi Iacobesco","René Bouloc","Jean Rougerie"],"genres":["drama","war"],"keywords":["war crimes","french gestapo","maquis","children in wartime"],"overview":"In Louis Malle's lauded drama, Lucien Lacombe is a young man living in rural France during World War II who seeks to join the French Resistance. When he is rejected due to his youth, the resentful Lucien allies himself with the Nazis and joins the Gallic arm of their Gestapo.","release_year":1974,"runtime_minutes":138,"original_language":"fr","poster_path":"/gHlorDyJrigxzcuZaQ5p4mseAPC.jpg","backdrop_path":"/ikO0koqdi0V7Z9CJXwwKf5tiTrs.jpg","tmdb_id":55368},
{"title":"Au Revoir les Enfants","original_title":"Au revoir les enfants","directors":["Louis Malle"],"cast_top":["Gaspard Manesse","Raphael Fejtö","Francine Racette","Stanislas Carré de Malberg","Philippe Morier-Genoud","François Berléand","François Négret","Peter Fitz"],"genres":["drama","war"],"keywords":["france","parent child relationship","resistance","vichy regime","holocaust (shoah)","world war ii","deportation","jew persecution","auschwitz-birkenau concentration camp","national socialism","biography","antisemitism","best friend","catholicism","resistance fighter"],"overview":"Au revoir les enfants tells a heartbreaking story of friendship and devastating loss concerning two boys living in Nazi-occupied France. At a provincial Catholic boarding school, the precocious youths enjoy true camaraderie—until a secret is revealed.","release_year":1987,"runtime_minutes":105,"original_language":"fr","poster_path":"/lXP90Vx7OcviBfbbokcaG6zVnPG.jpg","backdrop_path":"/xaRQqHgXMZCyqLFGZ7E3oDZx0ki.jpg","tmdb_id":1786},
