{"title":"Suzanne’s Career","original_title":"La Carrière de Suzanne","directors":["Éric Rohmer"],"cast_top":["Catherine Sée","Philippe Beuzen","Christian Charrière","Diane Wilkinson","Patrick Bauchau","Jean-Claude Biette","Jean-Louis Comolli","Pierre Cottrell"],"genres":["drama","romance"],"keywords":["paris","france","friends"],"overview":"In the second of Rohmer's moral tales, he examines the relationship between two friends and a girl who at first appears easily exploited. It is a complex tale of feelings and misconceptions, acted out within the head of the main character, as part of Rohmer's attempt to more easily simulate the mindscape quality of literature within a film.","release_year":1963,"runtime_minutes":54,"original_language":"fr","poster_path":"/5XNoOO5gmtSzFzPvPjy4OTY8sfe.jpg","backdrop_path":"/1AUOomyYHEaMrXZvSlaVNZhFw8a.jpg","tmdb_id":86764},
